{"page":3,"totalPages":4,"perPage":6,"nextPage":4,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/sudoku-solver.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/sudoku-solver.webp\" alt=\"A sudoku grid solved in the browser, with the solver’s digits picked out from the given ones\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2017-07-02T00:00:00.000Z\">2017.07.02</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/sudokusolver\">Sudoku solver</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A randomized constraint solver for Sudoku, ported from Python to JavaScript so it runs as you watch. Hand it a puzzle with more than one solution and it will cheerfully give you a different answer each time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Sudoku</li><li>Computing</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/orbit-camera.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/orbit-camera.webp\" alt=\"Coloured spheres over a mountain skybox, seen through the orbit camera\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2016-08-13T00:00:00.000Z\">2016.08.13</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/orbit-camera\">Orbit Camera for 3D scenes</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Most orbit controls rotate around a fixed origin, which starts to feel wrong the moment you zoom in on something off-centre. These controls pick whatever sits under your cursor as the object of interest and orbit around that instead.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>3D</li><li>camera</li><li>orbit</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/magic-square.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/magic-square.webp\" alt=\"A five by five magic square where every row, column and diagonal sums to 65\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2015-05-29T00:00:00.000Z\">2015.05.29</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>5 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/magicsquare\">Magic Squares</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">In a magic square of order n, every row, column and diagonal add up to the same number while using each of 1 through n squared exactly once. Here is how to build them, and why the odd, even and doubly even cases each need a trick of their own.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Magic Square</li><li>Computing</li><li>Mathematics</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/bezier-curve.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/bezier-curve.webp\" alt=\"A multi segment bezier curve with its draggable points and construction lines\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2015-04-16T00:00:00.000Z\">2015.04.16</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/bezier-curve\">Bezier curve playground</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Bezier curves are one of the few pieces of real mathematics the browser ships natively, which makes them a joy to play with. Drag the control points around and watch the construction lines sweep the curve into place.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>CSS</li><li>Bezier curves</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/circle-chords.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/circle-chords.webp\" alt=\"Chords drawn between periodic points on a circle, tracing out a cardioid\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2014-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2014.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/circle-chord-fun\">Fun with circle chords</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Draw a chord from point n to point 2n around a circle, repeat a few hundred times, and a cardioid appears out of nowhere. A small program I wrote so my kids could go hunting for the shapes hiding inside simple arithmetic.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Circle</li><li>Chords</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/Szilard-portrait.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/Szilard-portrait.webp\" alt=\"Portrait photograph of the physicist Leo Szilard\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2014-03-15T00:00:00.000Z\">2014.03.15</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>10 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/leo_szilard\">Leo Szilard - The Man who changed the World</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">He patented the nuclear chain reaction, drafted the letter that Einstein signed, and then spent the rest of his life trying to restrain the weapon he had set in motion. Leo Szilard may be the most consequential physicist you have never heard of.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Leo Szilard</li><li>Fission</li><li>Manhattan Project</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}